From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:00:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] macos: keep the window when a CEF webview is removed

Removing a CEF BrowserView closed the window it was in on macOS, with
the app's own webview and every other view in it. ElectrobunClient has
no DoClose, and CEF's default (false) sends performClose: to the
browser's top-level NSWindow once CloseBrowser runs; CEFWebViewImpl's
remove only takes the view out of its superview on the next turn of
the main queue, after CEF has found the window. Reproduced on stock
2.0.6: two windows, one CEF view each, removing either view emits the
window's close event.

A webview is always a child view (OnBeforePopup blocks popups), so
DoClose now returns true and the view's removal from the window
completes the browser close. During shutdown it keeps returning false,
as the Windows wrapper already does. Linux does not close the
top-level window on DoClose.
---
 package/src/native/macos/nativeWrapper.mm | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/src/native/macos/nativeWrapper.mm b/package/src/native/macos/nativeWrapper.mm
index 357de933..481e77ae 100644
--- a/package/src/native/macos/nativeWrapper.mm
+++ b/package/src/native/macos/nativeWrapper.mm
@@ -6937,6 +6937,16 @@ bool OnContextMenuCommand(CefRefPtr<CefBrowser> browser,
   // Life Span Handler
   CefRefPtr<CefLifeSpanHandler> GetLifeSpanHandler() override { return this; }
 
+  // A webview is a child view of an app window, never a window of its own
+  // (OnBeforePopup blocks popups). Returning false asks CEF to send
+  // performClose: to the NSWindow the view is in, so removing one CEF webview
+  // closed its whole window, with every other view in it. CEFWebViewImpl's
+  // remove takes the view out of the window, which completes the close.
+  // During shutdown keep CEF's own close sequence, as Windows does.
+  bool DoClose(CefRefPtr<CefBrowser> browser) override {
+    return !g_eventLoopStopping.load();
+  }
+
   bool OnBeforePopup(
       CefRefPtr<CefBrowser> browser, CefRefPtr<CefFrame> frame, int popup_id,
       const CefString &target_url, const CefString &target_frame_name,
